content.text:
That block is the site menu meant for phones, and a CSS rule is making it show on wide screens too. It came in with main's header rework (PR 2744) and is live on maester.dev, so PR 2678 didn't cause it. Merging main into this branch is what brought it into the preview.

**What's happening:** on phones the top bar folds away, so the docs sidebar repeats the site menu at its foot (Docs, Test catalog, Blog, Contributors and so on). In [Sidebar.astro](../maester-pr-2678/website/src/components/overrides/Sidebar.astro) that block is meant to hide on wide screens:

```astro
<nav class="mt-mobile-site md:sl-hidden" aria-label="Main">
```

Its own style, further down the same file, overrides that:

```css
.mt-mobile-site {
	display: grid;
	...
}
```

Starlight's `md:sl-hidden` class sits in a CSS cascade layer, and a plain style outside any layer always beats a layered one. So `display: grid` wins on every screen size. In the preview at 1400px wide, the menu block reports `display: grid` while every other `md:sl-hidden` element on the page reports `display: none`.

**The fix:** the topic tabs just above it in the same sidebar already handle this correctly: hidden by default, shown only under 50rem. The menu block needs the same pattern:

```css
.mt-mobile-site { display: none; ... }
@media (max-width: 49.99rem) {
	.mt-mobile-site { display: grid; }
}
```

It's a two-line change in one file.

